{14},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}=24.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample up to a constant $C.$\n\n*Hint: The probability mass function for a binomial random variable is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){\\theta }^{x}(1-\\theta )^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$" 13194139534771 17592186045417 true] [17592186435598 1072 #uuid "cec4340f-d49e-5a8e-a40d-7d35274dd0d2" 13194139534771 17592186045417 true] [17592186435598 1074 "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed discrete random variables with probability mass function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=P({X}_{1}={x}_{1},{X}_{2}={x}_{2},…,{X}_{n}={x}_{n})={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=14$ independent binomial random variables with unknown probability of success $\\theta $ and $N=6$ trials, for which the probability mass function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x;\\theta )=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{x}){\\theta }^{x}(1-\\theta )^{6-x}, & \\,x=0,1,2,…,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta ) \\\\  & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{i}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{i}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{i}} \\\\  & =((\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{1}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{1}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{1}})\\cdot ((\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{2}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{2}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{2}})⋯((\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{n}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{n}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{n}}) \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{\\,\\sum {x}_{i}}(1-\\theta )^{\\,\\sum (6-{x}_{i})} \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{\\,\\sum {x}_{i}}(1-\\theta )^{\\,6n-\\sum {x}_{i}} \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{S}(1-\\theta )^{6n-S}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{i}})$ is a constant and $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are told that $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=24$ and $n=14.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & =C\\,{\\theta }^{24}(1-\\theta )^{6(14)-24} \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{24}(1-\\theta )^{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534771 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1c1b5d67-2015-546a-b753-e86796910bb3" 17592186435559 "answer-29052ac4-071e-54fb-ae16-82067d8037d0" 17592186435560 "answer-389582af-a58f-54a7-ae30-7b904bf70c5c" 17592186435561 "answer-410f39b6-a584-5d06-bfad-158d3f61cf1c" 17592186435562 "answer-43ce76c4-9b3f-5e0d-8d4b-7dd6c7eb8a9b" 17592186435563 "answer-4b5112df-b8a5-508d-bd8d-84e15497dc00" 17592186435564 "answer-4e09edd5-72d9-50bc-b82f-3153d549f66b" 17592186435565 "answer-638f95eb-fe03-5c9c-b325-ab64d1a2bfb8" 17592186435566 "answer-71541f16-f169-5d86-b0ba-8063949a0c45" 17592186435567 "answer-72aacfd9-f2cf-5f0b-b080-dad3ce66cc66" 17592186435568 "answer-733053ef-496c-512e-b472-26d977bfe224" 17592186435569 "answer-74f9697a-0180-5e52-8045-a99af5573240" 17592186435570 "answer-7f861735-edd3-579d-a784-22d2d4cba82d" 17592186435571 "answer-838c6fad-c2ba-572a-946c-b271606a25e2" 17592186435572 "answer-8a6185d9-5090-58f9-9faf-f0ca13d18ad0" 17592186435573 "answer-93d50e3e-38b0-5f4f-9c02-3e8805be0a8e" 17592186435574 "answer-a64a48b1-2e38-5fa2-80c1-00ca67502114" 17592186435575 "answer-a69f56a5-8274-5d79-86ae-2334c516061c" 17592186435576 "answer-b25bf37a-582a-55f4-ac43-30454c204ab3" 17592186435577 "answer-c09dcbe2-1249-5a2a-a814-42f3694504c1" 17592186435578 "answer-c364aca3-b3e0-5c08-8833-f92f2c90e923" 17592186435579 "answer-c60c1729-d011-5a55-ab06-3140f2535dae" 17592186435580 "answer-da146878-2071-56de-b976-f02f6e1c86b4" 17592186435581 "answer-dd08ec01-50e9-52c6-8a79-0d3ad5f4d4fe" 17592186435582 "answer-deae0969-c9d6-5654-be64-6233a00a8a9b" 17592186435583 "answer-e346e105-c8a1-5024-ace6-a389edb0c7db" 17592186435584 "answer-e63ce25c-9077-5101-b2f1-edcd452a4672" 17592186435585 "answer-e763e4b4-79f2-57ef-a7b9-3f2fe750f